# Package-discovery and framework caches: regenerated by composer install /
# artisan, so a committed copy only ever describes the machine that last wrote
# it, and a stale one breaks artisan and the test suite wherever vendor/ differs
# (PR #319 review, F-026).
#
# main carried a blanket `bootstrap/` rule here. It is deliberately NOT kept
# (PR #319 review, F-033): it would also cover bootstrap/app.php, which is
# source, and bootstrap/cache/.gitignore, which is tracked on purpose as the
# keeper that makes the directory survive a clean checkout — without it the
# framework cannot boot (F-030). Worse, it made `git add` on that keeper a
# silent no-op, so the F-030 fix could not be committed at all. The rule below
# is scoped to the generated files only: it matches neither bootstrap/app.php
# nor bootstrap/cache/.gitignore.
/bootstrap/cache/*.php

